                <note rend="inline" type="source">353q116/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-15T13:00:00+00:00">January 15, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Department’s telegraphic instructions of January 14, 2 p.m. Decree objected to
                    by foreign missions has been indefinitely suspended; see Legation’s mail
                    despatches December 30 and January 2, respectively.<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d735-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
